  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-section">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What sports is CushionX designed for?</h3>
          <p>CushionX is built primarily for tennis, pickleball, and multi-sport courts, with applications for basketball and other cushioned athletic surfaces. It pairs cleanly with Acrytech Flex coatings for any sport-specific color or line configuration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do I know which thickness to choose?</h3>
          <p>4mm delivers a firmer, faster feel; 6mm is our most-requested "balanced" option; 8mm gives the most force reduction and is common on tennis and long-session pickleball courts. We'll recommend a thickness based on the sports you're playing, player preferences, and court use.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can CushionX be installed over my existing court?</h3>
          <p>Often, yes — provided the existing slab or asphalt base is structurally sound and properly sloped. We start with a free on-site evaluation to confirm the base is suitable and recommend any repair work needed before installation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How long does installation take?</h3>
          <p>A typical residential CushionX installation — including base prep, cushion application, coating, and line work — runs one to two weeks depending on scope and weather. The CushionX layer itself installs up to 3x faster than traditional cushioned systems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What about the warranty?</h3>
          <p>CushionX carries a 5-year manufacturer product warranty from AT Sports when the correct level is specified for the intended use and the system is installed to factory specification. We also back our workmanship separately. We'll review both warranties with you before the project starts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

